The Seller represents and warrants that:
(a) the financial statements are accurate;
(b) the Company is in material compliance with all applicable laws;
(c) to Seller's knowledge, there are no undisclosed liabilities save as disclosed in the Disclosure Letter;
(d) the Seller is not aware of any pending or threatened litigation regarding the Company, except as set out in the Disclosure Letter;
(e) all tax obligations of the Company are up to date and there are no outstanding notices of audit or assessment save as disclosed.
